---
// For Amazon sellers (Hashir, 17 Nov 2026): what OmniBridge reads and writes through the Selling
// Partner API and the Amazon Ads API, how a seller connects and disconnects, and how the data is
// kept (PRD 3.1, 3.2, 7.3). Wording drafted by S2 from the PRD; the client reviews it.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { CONTACT } from '../settings.ts';

const uses = [
  ['New and changed orders, with the delivery name, address and phone', 'To dispatch orders and print shipping labels'],
  ['Shipment confirmation and tracking numbers (written to Amazon)', 'So Amazon and your buyer see the order as dispatched'],
  ['Stock quantity on merchant-fulfilled listings (written to Amazon)', 'To keep one stock figure across Amazon and eBay'],
  ['Your listings report', 'To match your Amazon listings to your products'],
  ['Fees, transactions and settlements', 'To show profit per order and the VAT figures for your returns'],
  ['Account health, seller feedback and returns reports', 'To show account health and returns in one place'],
  ['Review requests (sent through Amazon)', 'To ask buyers for a review at the time Amazon allows'],
];
---

<Base
  title="For Amazon sellers"
  description="How OmniBridge connects to your Amazon seller account: what it reads and writes, how you connect and disconnect, and how buyer data is protected and deleted."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <h1>OmniBridge for Amazon sellers</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        How OmniBridge works with your Amazon seller account: what it reads and writes, how you connect
        and disconnect, and how your buyers’ data is protected.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose section-tail">
      <h2>What OmniBridge uses, and why</h2>
      <p>
        OmniBridge uses Amazon’s Selling Partner API with your permission. It reads and writes only what
        the features below need.
      </p>
      <div class="table-scroll">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Data</th><th>Why</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {uses.map(([data, why]) => (
              <tr><td>{data}</td><td>{why}</td></tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>
        Fulfilled by Amazon (FBA) listings and orders are shown read-only. OmniBridge never changes FBA
        stock.
      </p>

      <h2>Connecting your account</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>A workspace admin chooses the company and selects <strong>Connect Amazon</strong>.</li>
        <li>
          You sign in on Amazon’s own consent page and approve access there. OmniBridge never asks for,
          sees or stores your Amazon password.
        </li>
        <li>One Amazon seller account can be connected to only one OmniBridge workspace.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Disconnecting</h2>
      <p>
        You can disconnect in OmniBridge or remove the app’s access in Seller Central. All data from
        that Amazon account is then deleted within 30 days. The only exception is the finance records
        UK law requires us to keep, which contain no personal details.
      </p>

      <h2>How buyer data is protected</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Buyers’ delivery details are used only to dispatch their orders and answer them.</li>
        <li>They are kept in a separate encrypted database in Germany, with a key for each workspace.</li>
        <li>They are deleted from every copy, including backups, within 30 days of delivery.</li>
        <li>Every view of a buyer’s full details is logged.</li>
        <li>
          Buyer data is never sold, used for advertising, exported, or shared with another workspace.
        </li>
        <li>
          Every user of a workspace agrees to Amazon’s data rules in our <a href="/terms"
            >terms of service</a
          >.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Amazon Ads</h2>
      <p>
        Connecting Amazon Ads is optional and uses its own consent page. OmniBridge reads campaign
        reports as daily totals by campaign, ad group, keyword and product. It never reads data about
        individual shoppers. Ads data is used only inside your workspace, is visible only to the users
        you allow for that company, and is deleted within 30 days of disconnecting.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.support}`}>{CONTACT.support}</a>, or
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.privacy}`}>{CONTACT.privacy}</a> for data requests. Full details are
        in our <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
